# 7. DOCUMENT INGESTION PIPELINE

Implement asynchronous ingestion using RabbitMQ.

Workflow:

1. Admin uploads document.
2. Backend validates permissions and file.
3. Backend calculates SHA-256.
4. Backend creates document metadata.
5. Backend stores the original file securely.
6. Backend publishes an ingestion event.
7. Worker extracts document text.
8. Worker preserves page and section metadata.
9. Worker cleans extracted content.
10. Worker creates overlapping chunks.
11. Worker generates embeddings in batches.
12. Worker persists chunks and embeddings in pgvector.
13. Worker updates document status to INDEXED.
14. Worker records processing metrics.

Use reliable message acknowledgment, retry policies, dead-letter queues and idempotent processing.

Avoid embedding generation inside the HTTP upload request.

Support safe recovery from worker failures.

Do not mark a document INDEXED until its vectors and metadata have been successfully persisted.

