# 8. CHUNKING AND EMBEDDING

Implement configurable token-aware chunking.

Initial configuration:

- Chunk size: 800–1,000 tokens.
- Overlap: 100–150 tokens.
- Retrieval Top-K: 5.
- Similarity threshold: configurable.

These are starting defaults, not guaranteed optimal values.

Requirements:

- Preserve page numbers.
- Preserve document IDs.
- Preserve chunk IDs.
- Preserve section metadata.
- Avoid empty chunks.
- Avoid losing text at boundaries.
- Batch embedding requests.
- Validate embedding dimensions.
- Normalize vectors when required by the selected similarity strategy.
- Support embedding-model configuration.
- Record embedding model/version metadata.

Do not silently mix embeddings generated by incompatible models.

Implement a reindexing strategy for embedding-model changes.

