# 10. RAG ORCHESTRATION

Implement a dedicated RAG orchestration service.

Query workflow:

1. Authenticate the user.
2. Load conversation history.
3. Rewrite follow-up queries when necessary.
4. Generate query embeddings.
5. Retrieve authorized document chunks.
6. Apply similarity thresholds.
7. Optionally rerank results.
8. Build the grounded context.
9. Construct the LLM prompt.
10. Invoke the configured LLM.
11. Validate the generated response.
12. Resolve citations against actual retrieved chunks.
13. Calculate an evidence-based confidence category.
14. Persist the conversation and answer.
15. Record telemetry.
16. Return the structured response.

The LLM must never decide which documents a user is authorized to access.

Implement prompt-injection resistance.

Treat document content as untrusted input.

Do not allow instructions inside uploaded documents to override system-level instructions or authorization rules.

